    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0261" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/576: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-09T13:00:00+00:00">December 9, 1935—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 9—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. The London Naval Conference 1935 opened this morning at 10:30 and followed the
                    procedure outlined in the Embassy’s 581, November 21, 5 p.m. and 592, November
                    26, 6 p.m.<anchor n="99" xml:id="d151-f1"/> Following delivery of the opening
                    speeches the Conference resolved itself into committee of the whole called First
                    Committee which will meet tomorrow morning at 10:30 at Clifford House. Texts of
                    speeches being forwarded by mail.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d151-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d151-f1" n="99" xml:id="d151-f1-content">
                <p>Neither printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d151-f2" n="1" xml:id="d151-f2-content">
                <p>For texts of speeches, see The London Naval Conference, 1935, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Report of the Delegates of the United States</hi>, p.
                    48; the text of the speech delivered by the Chairman of the American delegation
                    is also printed in telegram No. 373, November 30, 1935, 4 p.m., to the
                    Ambassador in the United Kingdom, <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_281">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>, p. 281</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
